<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore's Hong Leong in US$40 mln bowling JV.</title>
<headline>Singapore's Hong Leong in US$40 mln bowling JV.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private property-based group Hong Leong Corp Ltd said on Monday it had set up a joint venture with America's AMF Bowling Worldwide to operate a chain of bowling centres in the Asia Pacific region.</p>
<p>A Hong Leong statement said the US$40 million joint venture, Hong Leong AMF Leisure Holdings Pte Ltd, would operate as many as 20 bowling centres over the next three years in Vietnam, Indonesia, Thailand, the Philippines, Malaysia and China.</p>
<p>Hong Leong and AMF would hold equal shares in the joint venture company. The first bowling centre would open in China this summer, the statement said.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
